values ('bbbb0004-0000-4000-8000-000000000037', 'en', null, 'Sports, Exercise and Health Science', 'Sports, Exercise and Health Science studies how the human body moves, fuels itself, and adapts to training, drawing on anatomy, physiology, biomechanics, nutrition, and the psychology of skill. This course follows the IB subject of the same name, covering the musculoskeletal, cardiovascular, and respiratory systems, energy systems, the principles of training, nutrition, movement analysis, motor learning, and the health and ethics of sport. Structure informed by Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia (CC BY-SA 4.0).', null, 'foundations', 53, true, 'science', '{}')
